{"parse":{"title":"spurtle","pageid":676767,"redirects":[],"text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"English\">English</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Alternative_forms\">Alternative forms</h3></div>\n<ul><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spirtle#English\" title=\"spirtle\">spirtle</a></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=spertle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"spertle (page does not exist)\">spertle</a></span> <span class=\"ib-brac qualifier-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content qualifier-content\">obsolete</span><span class=\"ib-brac qualifier-brac\">)</span></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_1\">Etymology 1</h3></div>\n<p>From <span class=\"etyl\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scots_language\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Scots language\">Scots</a></span> <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"sco\"><a class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" href=\"#Scots\">spurtle</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"sco\"><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=spurtill&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"spurtill (page does not exist)\">spurtill</a></i> <span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">(</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-double-quote\">“</span><span class=\"mention-gloss\">potstick, spatula</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-double-quote\">”</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">)</span>, of uncertain origin. Perhaps an alteration of <span class=\"etyl\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middle_English\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Middle English\">Middle English</a></span> <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\"><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=spatyl&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"spatyl (page does not exist)\">spatyl</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\"><a href=\"/wiki/spatule#Middle_English\" title=\"spatule\">spatule</a></i>, from <span class=\"etyl\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_French\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Old French\">Old French</a></span> <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\"><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=espatule&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"espatule (page does not exist)\">espatule</a></i> <span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">(</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-double-quote\">“</span><span class=\"mention-gloss\">spatula</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-double-quote\">”</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">)</span>. If so, then <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#doublet\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">doublet</a> of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spattle#English\" title=\"spattle\">spattle</a></i> and <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spatula#English\" title=\"spatula\">spatula</a></i>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Noun\">Noun</h4></div>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Spurtle.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Spurtle.jpg/250px-Spurtle.jpg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"190\" height=\"1500\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 0.75\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" srcset=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b3/Spurtle.jpg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x\" data-file-width=\"268\" data-file-height=\"2116\" /></a><figcaption>A porridge <b>spurtle</b>.</figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"interproject-box sister-wikipedia sister-project noprint floatright\"><div style=\"float: left;\" class=\"interproject-box-logo\"><figure class=\"mw-halign-none\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Wikipedia-logo-v2.svg/60px-Wikipedia-logo-v2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"44\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Wikipedia-logo-v2.svg/120px-Wikipedia-logo-v2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"103\" data-file-height=\"94\" /></span><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div><div style=\"margin-left: 60px;\">English <a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia\" title=\"Wikipedia\">Wikipedia</a> has an article on:<div style=\"margin-left: 10px;\"><b class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/spurtle\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:spurtle\">spurtle</a></b></div></div><span class=\"interProject\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/spurtle\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:spurtle\">Wikipedia </a></span></div><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r86621275\">.mw-parser-output .interproject-box{font-size:90%;width:250px;padding:5px;text-align:left;background:var(--wikt-palette-paleblue,#f9f9f9);border:var(--border-color-base,#aaa)1px solid;display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center}.mw-parser-output .interproject-box-logo{min-width:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.mw-parser-output .interproject-box>div:first-child{float:none!important;flex:none}.mw-parser-output .interproject-box>div:nth-child(2){margin-left:0.55em!important}body.skin-vector:not(.skin-vector-2022) .mw-parser-output .interproject-box .vector-hide{display:none}body.skin-vector:not(.skin-vector-2022) .mw-parser-output .interproject-box .vector-inline-block{display:inline-block;margin-left:0!important}@media screen and (max-width:719px){.mw-parser-output .interproject-box{box-sizing:border-box;line-height:1.5;width:100%;max-width:100%;padding:6px}}</style>\n<p><span class=\"headword-line\"><strong class=\"Latn headword\" lang=\"en\">spurtle</strong> (<i>plural</i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en p-form-of\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spurtles#English\" title=\"spurtles\">spurtles</a></b>)</span>\n</p>\n<ol><li>Either of two <a href=\"/wiki/Scottish\" title=\"Scottish\">Scottish</a> <a href=\"/wiki/kitchen\" title=\"kitchen\">kitchen</a> <a href=\"/wiki/implement\" title=\"implement\">implements</a> made of <a href=\"/wiki/wood\" title=\"wood\">wood</a>: a flat one for turning oatcakes, or a stick for stirring porridge.\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1850</b></span>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Keightley\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Thomas Keightley\">Thomas Keightley</a>, <cite>The Fairy Mythology</cite>, London&#58; H.G. Bohn, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">353</span>:</span><dl><dd><div class=\"h-quotation\"><span class=\"Latn e-quotation cited-passage\" lang=\"en\">\"It was till lately believed by the ploughmen of Clydesdale, that if they repeated the rhyme<br />&#160;&#160;&#160;Fairy, fairy, bake me a bannock and roast me a collop,<br />&#160;&#160;&#160;And I'll gie ye a <b>spurtle</b> off my gadend&#33;<br />three several times on turning their cattle at the terminations of ridges, they would find the said fare prepared for them on reaching the end of the fourth furrow.\"</span></div></dd></dl></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1997</b></span>, Charles Frazier, <cite>Cold Mountain</cite>, London&#58; Hodder and Stoughton, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">311</span>:</span><dl><dd><div class=\"h-quotation\"><span class=\"Latn e-quotation cited-passage\" lang=\"en\">One day they built a fire in the yard and made a black kettle of apple butter so big that when they stood over it and stirred the apple mash with <b>spurtles</b>, the scene put Ada in mind of the witches in Macbeth working at their brew.</span></div></dd></dl></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading5\"><h5 id=\"Translations\">Translations</h5></div>\n<div class=\"NavFrame\" id=\"Translations-kitchen&#95;implement\"><div class=\"NavHead\" style=\"text-align:left\">kitchen implement</div><div class=\"NavContent\"><table class=\"translations\" role=\"presentation\" data-gloss=\"kitchen implement\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"translations-cell multicolumn-list\" colspan=\"3\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r87480995\">.mw-parser-output .translations{width:100%;margin:0}.mw-parser-output .translations-cell{background-color:var(--wikt-palette-lightyellow,#FFFFe0);vertical-align:top;text-align:left}</style>\n<ul><li>Polish: <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"pl\"><a href=\"/wiki/drewniany#Polish\" title=\"drewniany\">drewniany</a> <a href=\"/wiki/kij#Polish\" title=\"kij\">kij</a> <a href=\"/wiki/do#Polish\" title=\"do\">do</a> <a href=\"/wiki/mieszanie#Polish\" title=\"mieszanie\">mieszania</a> <a href=\"/wiki/owsianka#Polish\" title=\"owsianka\">owsianki</a></span>&#160;<span class=\"gender\"><abbr title=\"masculine gender\">m</abbr>&#160;<abbr title=\"inanimate\">inan</abbr></span></li></ul>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_2\">Etymology 2</h3></div>\n<p>From <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spurt#English\" title=\"spurt\">spurt</a></i> +&#8206; <i class=\"Latn mention nowrap\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/-le#English:_frequentative\" title=\"-le\">-le</a></i>.\nAccording to the Poly-Olbion project, <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#coinage\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">coined</a> by poet <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Drayton\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Michael Drayton\">Michael Drayton</a> in 1606.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Verb\">Verb</h4></div>\n<p><span class=\"headword-line\"><strong class=\"Latn headword\" lang=\"en\">spurtle</strong> (<i>third-person singular simple present</i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en s-verb-form-form-of\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spurtles#English\" title=\"spurtles\">spurtles</a></b>, <i>present participle</i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en ing-form-form-of\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spurtling#English\" title=\"spurtling\">spurtling</a></b>, <i>simple past and past participle</i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en ed-form-form-of\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spurtled#English\" title=\"spurtled\">spurtled</a></b>)</span>\n</p>\n<ol><li>To <a href=\"/wiki/spurt\" title=\"spurt\">spurt</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/spatter\" title=\"spatter\">spatter</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/sputter\" title=\"sputter\">sputter</a>; to <a href=\"/wiki/spurt\" title=\"spurt\">spurt</a> in a <a href=\"/wiki/scatter\" title=\"scatter\">scattering</a> manner.\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1612</b></span>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Drayton\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Michael Drayton\">Michael Drayton</a>, <cite><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poly-Olbion\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Poly-Olbion\">Poly-Olbion</a></cite>, <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://poly-olbion.exeter.ac.uk/the-text/words/spirtle/\">song 2 p. 29</a></span>:</span><dl><dd><div class=\"h-quotation\"><span class=\"Latn e-quotation cited-passage\" lang=\"en\">Upon the head hee lent so violent a stroke,<br />That the poore emptie skull, like some thin potsheard broke,<br />The braines and mingled blood, were <b>spertled</b> on the wall</span></div></dd></dl></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<ul><li><i>Oxford English Dictionary</i>, 2nd edition (1989)</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://poly-olbion.exeter.ac.uk/the-text/words/spirtle/\">The Poly-Olbion project</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Anagrams\">Anagrams</h3></div>\n<ul><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/spurlet#English\" title=\"spurlet\">spurlet</a></span>, <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/Purtles#English\" title=\"Purtles\">Purtles</a></span></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐web.eqiad.main‐5c5554d4b‐ldhgs\nCached time: 20260924080703\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, prevent‐selective‐update, show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.286 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.395 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 376/1000000\nRevision size: 2561/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 13996/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 6/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 8/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1347/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.226/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 14168132/104857600 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  373.136      1 -total\n 41.79%  155.915      2 Template:alt\n 11.13%   41.548      3 Template:quote-book\n  6.53%   24.357      1 Template:bor\n  6.14%   22.916      1 Template:wp\n  6.05%   22.572      1 Template:en-noun\n  5.10%   19.039      1 Template:inh\n  3.99%   14.876      1 Template:t\n  3.42%   12.745      1 Template:trans-top\n  3.08%   11.503      1 Template:suf\n-->\n\n<!-- Render ID ece9365a-b7ee-11f1-ac74-87946bb91d04 -->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key enwiktionary:pcache:676767:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20260924080703 and revision id 91214334. Rendering was triggered because: page_view\n -->\n</div>"}}